2026-09-27 — bounded recursive visitor substitution.

RED: the existing five private-leaf regressions pass, but two added tests fail:
the visitor stays out of line because its runtime call graph is cyclic, and
ordinary inline substitution ignores an earlier noinline declaration.
This is not a parser or validator suppression.

Repair: distinguish runtime recursion from finite substitution. An unaddressed
internal inline function with one source call in an ineligible, non-inline
caller can be expanded without expanding its recursive call back to that
caller. The existing C-HIR machinery retains parameter conversion, fresh local
object identity, lifetimes, labels and effects. Admission is bounded at 1024
unexpanded nodes and 256 bytes of fixed local objects; variadics, assembly,
statics, address-taken labels, dynamic allocation and activation-sensitive
builtins remain ordinary calls. No new IR, implicit state or EqSat rule.
All optional substitution paths also honor noinline/noipa/noclone throughout
the declaration chain; mandatory always_inline semantics remain unchanged.

Nine CLI tests pass, including both interpreters and validated IR at O0/O2:
  - recursive three-way visitor: 120 callbacks, before/after values and early
    error return remain correct; visitor call/body removed, walker call retained;
  - all three barriers before/after the definition retain the call;
  - multiple callers, inline caller, taken address, static storage, >256 bytes,
    VLA, alloca, frame address and >1024 nodes stay outside admission;
  - actual inlining preserves lifetime E3010, uninitialized E3001 and division
    by zero E3002 in both interpreters.
The unchanged fixture exits zero in sealed GCC14/Clang19/EvoCC O0/O2: 6/6.

Exact original arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/pgtable.o replay uses its .o.cmd and actual
generated headers from the retained expanded configuration. Both before/after
objects assemble and match all global symbol names/kinds. The visit definition
and call disappear; the recursive walk remains. Text 33068 -> 32964 bytes;
data remains 1000 bytes. Neither object was installed. This is not a measured
runtime speedup and does not close K02/K03.

The before compiler is a debug executable; the after is release. Their compile
times are therefore NOT an inlining-speed comparison. The full-build launch
using that debug executable was interrupted before completing its first batch
or installing objects. Its INTERRUPTED receipt is retained; there is no claim
that it passed. A verified frozen release is used for the next uniform build.

